Dogs and cats don't eat lichen corpses or rations, but the player can eat
them safely.
The general rule for corpses is that most of them are edible IF YOU EAT
THEM WHILE THEY ARE STILL FRESH! You shouldn't eat corpses that have been
dead for more than about 50 turns. And if you didn't see it die, it is
probably already rotten and too old to eat.
There are exceptions to this rule of the thumb: for example lichen and
acid blob corpses never get too old to eat. And there are some other
corpses that are never safe to eat.

